undamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Louisiana remains a deeply Republican state in presidential politics, and the 2028 open-seat contest begins with that structural advantage on the Republican side. No incumbent is on the ballot because the sitting president is term-limited, which removes any personal incumbency effect while leaving the state's partisan foundations intact. No public general-election polls, expert ratings, or market pricing are available yet, so the outlook rests on the state's fundamental lean.\n\nHeadlines so far concern prospective candidates rather than the state itself: Kamala Harris has engaged with Louisiana redistricting while remaining undecided about a run, and Senator John Kennedy has floated a Republican bid. Neither development changes the underlying arithmetic. The Republican nominee is strongly favored to carry the state, with meaningful uncertainty only because the campaign has not yet produced measurable data.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.108, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.162, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1608, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1621, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1551, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.153, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.155, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1556, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1525, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1509, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1527, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1593, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.156, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.155, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1523, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.1512, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.1525, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.14